    "description": "Lead Software Engineer. As software lead, I lead the DO-178B software design and development efforts for the Boeing 787 Power Electronics Cooling System (PECS), and 787 Nitrogen Generation System (NGS). Activities included performing as well as overseeing the design and development of software to control the 787PECS, and NGS. Participated as Software Control Board (SCB) Leader where I lead a cross functional team consisting of Software, Systems, Project and Quality Engineers. SCB activities which included: approving requirements, performing and approving reviews, approving changes, and risk mitigation.  Interfaced with customer on a regular basis, as well as participated in Preliminary Design Reviews, Critical Design Review, and Stages of Involvement audits.\nProvided oversight to offshore outsource supplier performing verification activities including code reviews, structural coverage analysis and unit testing, and requirements base testing.\nDuring my time on the project I became more knowledgeable on the development of complex software algorithms, Source Control, Software Testing tasks, reporting and analysis of software metrics, and software documentation.  During this time, I learned how to manage working a high-pressure schedule with rapidly changing requirements due to integration testing’s feedback, meanwhile being required to always meet the schedule deadlines.  I also participated on FAA certification of software and testing tools. At the end of the project I participated in Kaizen and the project Lessons Learn on meetings to assure the continued improvement of all future projects. \n",
